Assert the whole corpus is a fixpoint of the compact form

Dev accepted, in these words: "Accepted, build it" — the recommendation being one new ResolutionRecordTest
case walking every definition under src/main/resources and src/mods/resources, choosing the resolution scope
by package, and asserting for each that its compact form encodes to the definition itself and that the
compact form reads back to the same resolution; no engine change, no definition or committed Scala change,
no new suite.

Why. The record of ed57aa9 (the anchor-parameter rule) said why its defect met no gate: no test compacts
the example definitions, and the two-stage loader never re-reads its own result. That was still the shape
of the suite after ed57aa9. ResolutionRecordTest pinned unscoped equals scoped generation over the main
corpus, and the compact round trip of four definitions by name (Percept, Waypoint, Ego, TypeDictionary).
The claim the two sweeps made — 2026-10-21 for the canonical and staged corpus (132 definitions), 2026-10-31
for the twelve example definitions the compact form changes — that every definition IS the compact form was
measured in their records and asserted nowhere as a whole. DRACO.md §1 names the goal: a measurement becomes
an assertion, and the table shrinks.

