under the two resource roots other than the nameless domain's anchor: 183 definitions; 183 whose compact
form encodes to the definition itself (`scope.compact(td)` equal to `td`); 183 whose compact form reads back
(`scope.resolve(compact)` equal to `scope.resolve(td)`). The scope is the one each definition's caller
supplies — `CanonicalScope.scope` for draco (the canonical identity ontology and HostBindings' vocabulary),
the example caller's `NameResolution` over `ExampleScope.declarations` and `ExampleScope.bindings` for
