full and `anchorParameter` wrote it bare again, this test fails on both; it is the gate the record of
ed57aa9 found missing.

Built as measured. ResolutionRecordTest gains its sixth case, "the whole corpus is a fixpoint of the compact
form: every definition under main and mods compacts to itself and reads back": the walk, the two scopes, the
two assertions per definition each naming the stem that fails, and a lower bound on the count — at least
183, as the suite's whole-corpus generation case bounds the main corpus at 110 — so a definition cannot drop
out of the walk silently while an added type does not fail the gate. Nothing else changes: no engine line,
no definition, no committed Scala. The test reads the resource roots directly, as the suite's other cases
do, and asks nothing of the classpath.

